Do not generate PWA icons at build time (drop vite-plugin-pwa pwaAssets).

The pwaAssets generator (preset minimal-2023) runs
@vite-pwa/assets-generator on sharp with its prebuilt libvips
binaries to render icon variants. Nothing else in the tree uses
sharp: no workspace depends on it and no source imports it, so
without this option the generator module is never imported and
sharp never loads. The generated icons (pwa-192x192.png and
friends) are gone from the PWA output; the manifest text and the
precache of every other asset are unchanged. The two consumers
of the generated icon now use the static app icon that the UI
build already stages as public/logo.png: the packaged-resources
smoke check and the Windows toast identity (test path updated
to match).

